    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds pretty definitive. but what about the actual physical and economic hurdles? i'm hearing a lot of talk about grid instability, the massive shortage of minerals like lithium and copper, and just the sheer cost of replacing existing infra. shouldn't those be considered major counter-arguments to the \"inevitability\" idea?",
