      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the political and regulatory momentum is strong, the physical and economic hurdles you mentioned are the single biggest risk factors to the timeline of the transition. Grid instability and a 40-50% rise in land and installation costs make the shift significantly more expensive than often predicted in optimistic models, while a shortage of rare critical minerals can push up the cost of renewable energy without a guaranteed outcome. Although the total system capital expenditure is likely too great to abandon fossil fuels entirely, those specific bottlenecks mean that a complete \"done deal\" today is unlikely because the transition depends on solving these engineering and supply chain problems before they become financial showstoppers.",
